<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keoladeo National Park</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bharatpur Bird Sanctuary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keoladeo National Park is a wetland reserve next to Bharatpur in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Created in the 19th century as a duck-shooting preserve of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharajas</a> of Bharatpur, it became a national park in 1982 and a World Heritage Site in 1985. It is one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>'s most important wintering grounds for waterbirds, formerly including the Siberian crane.</p></div>
